it to a specific pawn structure yet\n- It attacks the center and prepares further piece development\n\nReason: N: g1-f3 is the most natural and strong developing move. It brings the knight to its ideal square where it controls key central squares, defends the e4 pawn, and prepares for safe kingside castling. This move is consistent with sound opening principles: develop pieces quickly, control the center, and prepare to castle. It's also the starting move of many strong opening systems.\n\nAnswer: N: g1-f3"}
