gside. This fits well with many sound opening principles.\n- **B: f1-b5**: The Ruy Lopez/Spanish setup, pinning the knight.\n\nReason: I'll choose **B: f1-c4** because it develops a piece actively, puts immediate pressure on Black's weakest point (f7), maintains flexibility in the position, and prepares kingside castling. This move is consistent with the Italian Game opening principles and creates immediate tactical threats while maintaining good development.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
