 d5-b6 and N: d5-c7 both fork queen and rook but don't give check\n\nReason: N: d5-e7 is the strongest move because it delivers check to the Black king on f7 while simultaneously attacking the queen on d8. This is a classic royal fork. Black must respond to the check, and will likely have to move the king, after which I can capture the queen with Nxd8, dramatically improving my position. This is the most forcing continuation and gives me the best practical chances in an otherwise losing position.\n\nAnswer: N: d5-e7"}
